## Composer vs Standard Chat

### Key Differences

| Aspect | Composer (Cmd+K/L) | Standard Chat |
|--------|-------------------|---------------|
| **Context** | Auto-includes selected code, open files | User must manually reference files |
| **Output** | Can directly edit code in editor | Generates text in chat bubble |
| **Execution** | Can run tools, files, and terminal commands | Text-only responses |
| **Shortcuts** | Keyboard-driven workflow | Mouse-driven interface |
| **Integration** | Deeply integrated with editor | Standalone panel |
| **Use case** | Code modification, quick fixes | Exploration, explanation, planning |

### When to Use Each

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Need AI assistance] --> B{What type of action?}
    B -->|Modify code| C[Cmd+K Inline Edit]
    B -->|Explain or chat| D[Cmd+L Side Panel]
    B -->|Generate new file| E[Cmd+L with /new]
    B -->|Quick fix| F[Cmd+K with /fix]
    B -->|Test generation| G[Cmd+K with /test]
    C --> H[Select code first]
    D --> I[Type question]
    E --> J[Describe file content]
    F --> K[Select buggy code]
    G --> L[Select code to test]
```

